      {
        "position": 2,
        "title": "Must have emergency pet carrier sling",
        "text": "This packable lift harness is exactly what I needed for piece of mind for emergencies. It is very much for emergency use in my household, but of course I had to test it out with my 15 lb pup first. She thankfully really didn't mind it. It took a minute to get her secured in there, but it was clear that it fit her snugly and I could move around really easily wearing the sling. It's a really great idea to have this for a dog or cat for natural disaster preparedness. I think it's absolutely worth the price. My pup felt really comfortable and we were able to move around and go for a walk without any discomfort for her or myself. She wasn't able to even attempt to get out. I think she felt really safe. The straps are very easy to adjust and tighten. There is a nice carrying case that comes with it. It's super well made and I think would last a few day trek if you needed to carry your animal a long. distance. I am so happy to have this for piece of mind!",
        "rating": 5,
        "date": "May 24, 2026",
        "author": "Salish",
        "author_link": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AHDT3WQ7F6QLHTLKQSGDBVISCAUQ?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top",
        "author_image": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/default._SX48_.png",
        "product": {
          "size": "L（18.5-29.5lbs）",
          "color": "Black"
        }
      },
      {
        "position": 3,
        "title": "Your pet will feel safe in this carrier.",
        "text": "This is an extremely well made, strong carrier. My dog felt completely at ease and supported. He is a 10lb maltipom. I am returning it because it will take too long to put on while on our walks. It will also be too hot in FL.",
        "rating": 4,
        "date": "April 26, 2026",
        "author": "Cynsroom",
        "author_link": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AHBU6EWA7C26DELCRK7GFNB42F7Q?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top",
        "author_image": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/default._SX48_.png",
        "helpful_votes": "One person found this helpful",
        "verified_purchase": true,
        "product": {
          "size": "M（8.5-17.5lbs）",
          "color": "Black"
        }
      },
      {
        "position": 4,
        "title": "Great for cats too",
        "text": "I ordered this sling for my big 15lb cats. I wanted a kind of \"cat handle\" I could use in situations where I need to care for my cats in ways they don't like such as giving pills, trimming nails, etc. One of my cats requires occasional enemas and it's very difficult to hold her in position to wash off her poopy little butt after the enema. This sling makes all of these things so much easier. After she's in the sling I can hold her in place with one hand and use my other hand to wash her butt or give her a pill.I also plan to use this to take her outside for fresh air but still have her secure if I need to grab her off the ground quickly. I can attach a leash to the sling and let her hang out on the ground and then just lift her up by the sling if necessary. The sling makes it easy to go on little walks with her comfortably sitting in the sling in front of me. I feel like it is a much better way to let her enjoy the fresh air rather than to cram her into a little enclosed backpack or something.The sling is very well made with solid stitching throughout. The buckles are easy to open and close and adjust and the medium size fits my 15lb cats well. I feel like my cats are very safe and secure when they are in the sling. The sling comes with a compact 12\" x 6\" storage bag and it is easy to quickly deploy when needed. Overall I'm very happy with the sling and am glad I ordered it.",
        "rating": 5,
        "date": "April 18, 2026",
