        "title": "Great fit",
        "text": "I got this for my Frenchie with early IVDD. He also has a non-operable injured leg from when he was 6 months old and we wear a brace when we go to the park. He loves to chase the ball but he limps pretty bad towards the end of his plays. I wanted a sling for him that was easy to pack for that just-in-case so I had some peace of mind. I ordered an XL and he’s 37 pounds, so heavier than the max weight. It worked great and was simple to put on. He was really calm in it, and it was easy to get over my shoulders. It came in a packable little bag, so easy to store. If I had to say one thing negative, there’s not much padding on the shoulders, so with how heavy He is, my shoulders hurt after a fairly short time. But this will be for emergencies for us, and for that it works great.",
